<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      THE LAUNCHER NAME IS A VOICE TARGET, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS ONE WORD.

      This is the name Google matches when somebody says "open X" or "play
      something on X", and "MusicD Remote Lite" lost on every count: three
      words to say, and a trailing capital letter that no speech model has a
      place for. It came back as "Music d remote light" and resolved to
      nothing. The rule the failure teaches is short, ordinary, and spelled
      the way it sounds.

      KNOWN COST, ACCEPTED DELIBERATELY. "Remote" is a common word, and other
      things on a phone answer to something like it — Android TV Remote
      Service, Roon's own app, whatever else is installed. An exact match
      should win over those, but it is a gamble on Google's matcher rather
      than a guarantee, and it was taken with that understood.

      The project is still MusicD Remote Lite: the package, the repository and
      the name Roon shows in Settings -> Extensions are all unchanged. This is
      only what the launcher icon and the Assistant call it.
    -->
    <string name="app_name">Remote</string>
    <string name="dial_name">Dial for Roon</string>
    <string name="tile_random_album">Random album</string>

    <!-- The plain bar widget. -->
    <string name="widget_bar_description">Now playing, with transport. Tap the cover for a random album.</string>

    <!--
      The dial widget. These two names are fixed by the layout synced from
      Dial for Roon, so they are what they are; see tools/dial-upstream.json.
    -->
    <string name="widget_artwork">Album artwork</string>
    <string name="widget_description">The dial: album art in a volume ring, with transport and volume.</string>
</resources>
